%% Figure 2 - Host certificate authentication flow (TOFU eliminated)
%% Source of truth: docs/technical-reference.md, Section 4
%% Render: mmdc -i 02-host-cert-flow.mmd -o 02-host-cert-flow.png
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    participant C as SSH Client<br/>(ssh-client 10.222.9.30)
    participant S as SSH Server<br/>(server.lab.local 10.222.9.20)
    participant CA as Host CA<br/>(offline / Cosmian KMS)

    note over CA,S: One-time provisioning<br/>(before any client connects)
    CA ->> S: Sign host key with Host CA<br/>(ssh-keygen -h -n server.lab.local,IP)
    note over S: Install ssh_host_ed25519_key-cert.pub<br/>HostCertificate in sshd_config

    note over C: Trust the Host CA ONCE<br/>@cert-authority *.lab.local ecdsa... in known_hosts

    C ->> S: TCP connect + SSH version exchange
    S -->> C: Host key + host certificate<br/>(ssh-ed25519-cert-v01)

    note over C: 1. Extract CA key from cert<br/>2. Match @cert-authority pattern<br/>3. Verify CA signature<br/>4. Check hostname in principals<br/>5. Check validity window

    alt Certificate trusted
        C -->> C: No TOFU prompt -<br/>server identity proven
        C ->> S: Proceed to user authentication
    else Bad / untrusted cert
        C -->> C: Reject connection<br/>(no silent accept)
    end
